# Local-only: copy of the OpenAT template kept for reference, not published.
_template_reference/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Oversized media: kept locally, not published to git
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The three tutorial recordings are 368-705 MB each. GitHub hard-rejects any
# single file over 100 MB, and Git LFS's free tier is 1 GB total, so mirroring
# 1.5 GB of video here would cost money and make every clone enormous. All
# three are already published on YouTube (linked from README.md and from
# Video_Tutorials/README.md), which is where viewers actually watch them.
#
# What IS published: the .srt subtitle files, the step-by-step screenshots, the
# transcript-derived written walkthrough, and the video index. Someone with no
# internet access still gets the full procedure in text and images.
Video_Tutorials/**/*.mp4
Video_Tutorials/**/*.avi
Video_Tutorials/**/*.mov

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Redundant CAD copies: Design_Files/CAD_Design_Files/ is the published tree
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Braille_Embosser_CAD_Design_Files/ is a byte-identical copy of
# CAD_Design_Files/ plus a zip of the Fusion archive it already contains, and
# Braille_Embosser_CAD_Design_Files.zip is a zip of that. Publishing all three
# would add ~266 MB of duplicates to every clone. The local copies stay put.
Design_Files/Braille_Embosser_CAD_Design_Files/
Design_Files/Braille_Embosser_CAD_Design_Files.zip

